                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Being fascinated by early and old hardware and software, I have always enjoyed the aesthetic of the old dos platformers like Commander Keen, Duke Nukem and Bio Menace and the likes, but one thing those games fail to have is modern quality of life. Often fixed by source ports, but those aren't always available or the best. \n\nMuri, on top of being an amazingly designed video game with beautiful retro art and fun gameplay, invokes the feeling of how people \"remember\" those old games. smooth, easy to run, challenging but fair, and overall just a blast to play through. \n\nA love letter to DOS Platforming through and through, and if you like the sound of that, you owe it to yourself to play this game.",
